<div id="content">
  <h3 class="linklist">Bolex Reporter, Volume 9</h3>
  <!-- EPHEMERA and bolex reporter stuff -->
  <div id="books"> 
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltright" src="../images/reporter/09_1.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="285"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">Winter 1958</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 9, Number 1</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "Ten Tips for Winter Movies"; 
        "Superimpose Your Titles"; "An Introduction to Home Movies", Raymond C. 
        Lawson; "Winter Project: Silhouette Movies", Russell T. Christopher; "Hunting 
        with a Bolex", Warren Page; "Movie of an Inanimate Subject", Paul Dana; 
        "Composition for Wide Screen Movies", Ernst Wildi</li>
      <li class="desc">The results of the Bolex Film Festival are announced. Raymond 
        C. Lawson begins the first in a ten part series of articles on home movie 
        making; these articles were later compiled into a <a href="books60.html">small 
        booklet</a> of the same name.</li>
      <li class="pp">32 pages</li>
    </ul>
    <hr>
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/reporter/09_2.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="280"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">Spring 1959</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 9, Number 2</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "Plan A Travelogue", Derek 
        Hill; "Through the Kaleidoscope", Weegee; "An Introduction to Home Movies 
        (Part II)", Raymond C. Lawson; "Let Color Work For You", Barton Ford; 
        "Now is the Time to Start Family Movies", Ted Russell; "Decamired Color 
        Filter System", Ernst Wildi; "Show Growth and Change with Time Lapse", 
        Jack Ruddell; "The Money Machine", Ray Dantzler; "Spring Service", Fred 
        Onderka; "Animated Cartoon TV Commercials with Bolex", David Bennett</li>
      <li class="desc">Weegee returns to discuss more of his kaleidoscope filming 
        technique. The H-16 REX, C-8SL, B-8SL, rexofader and switar 13mm f/0.9 
        are introduced and reviewed.</li>
      <li class="pp">32 pages</li>
    </ul>
    <hr>
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltright" src="../images/reporter/09_3.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="280"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">Summer 1959</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 9, Number 3</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "How to Edit Your Films", 
        Jack Ruddell; "Bolex Goes to a 'Fiesta de Toros'", Vincent Kehoe; "An 
        Introduction to Home Movies (Part III)", Raymond C. Lawson; "Come On In! 
        The Water's Fine", Ray Dantzler; "Mom Films a Birthday Greeting", Lou 
        Lachter; "Movies Help Teach Water Skills", Harold Hainfeld; "...Of Sailing 
        Boats and Movie Films...", Lloyd S. Jones; "Make Animated Cartoons With 
        Your Bolex", Fredric Stoessell; "Bolex Helps Keep Pace With Space Age", 
        Lt. Cecil Stoughton; "How to Make Fades, Wipes, Dissolves", Ernst Wildi; 
        "Stairway to the Stars", Tom Sulliivan</li>
      <li class="desc">This summer issue is full of tips for the amateur and professional 
        Bolex user. The new D-8L and Pan Cinor 85 is introduced.</li>
      <li class="pp">32 pages</li>
    </ul>
    <hr>
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/reporter/09_4.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="283"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">Fall 1959</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 9, Number 4</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "Take Movies From Your Car", 
        George Nagorsky; "Available Light Movies", David S. Brown; "Make-Up for 
        Home Movies", Barton Ford; "Filming a Speech Camp", Bob Newman; "...The 
        Best is Yet to Come (Fall Movies)", Alan Arnold; "Movies: Tool For Football 
        Coaches", Harold Hainfeld; "Sports Cars on Film", Myron A. Matzkin; "Shoot 
        a Solar Eclipse", Peter Leavens; "How to Make Sharp 8mm Movies", Ernst 
        Wildi; "Camera Magic", Tom Sullivan; "An Introduction to Home Movies (Part 
        IV), Raymond C. Lawson; "Creative Use of Lenses", Ira Latour</li>
      <li class="desc">The Declic D, Tripod H, Unimotor MC-17, Pan Cinor 30L (8mm), 
        Pizar 50mm f/1.8 and Switar 36mm f/1.8 (d mount) is introduced.</li>
      <li class="pp">32 pages</li>
    </ul>
